00:00:19,690 --> 00:00:30,510
Mosquitoes are the deadliest animals to humans. Around 700,000 people die every year due to mosquito-borne diseases such as malaria, Zika virus, dengue and yellow fever.

6
00:00:31,210 --> 00:00:40,340
Due to climate change and the associated global warming, mosquitoes are opening up more and more habitats and will spread drastically over the coming years, along with the diseases they transmit.

7
00:00:41,250 --> 00:00:51,310
To hinder the spread of these diseases, several prevention strategies have been developed, such as insecticides as a vector control or mosquito repellents for dermatological use.

8
00:00:51,910 --> 00:00:59,500
