10
00:01:04,580 --> 00:01:07,440
Heron repellents are based on the substance DEET.

11
00:01:08,100 --> 00:01:17,710
Unfortunately, its production is based on crude oil and produces a lot of toxic byproducts, which makes the process environmentally harmful and unsustainable.

12
00:01:18,340 --> 00:01:19,980
But here we present an alternative.

13
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:32,500
The structurally similar molecule, NBP, is a promising mosquito repellent and can be produced in microorganisms. So we decided to work with coronobacterium glutamicum as it's ultimately based on a minor acid.

14
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:49,200
To build the body of our project, we first had to lay the foundation for a fomentative production. And as MVP is currently not synthesized in any organism, we had to develop an artificial pathway using enzymes from several different organisms.

15
00:01:49,730 --> 00:01:57,010
This pathway is based on the two common amino acids, lysine and phenylalanine, which are then refined to form piperidine and benzoate, respectively.

16
00:01:57,670 --> 00:02:01,260
These two molecules are then combined to form our bio repellent NBP.

17
00:02:03,590 --> 00:02:14,130
For this pathway, we generated several constructs for the expression in corona bacteria and glutamicome, contributing to the implementation of this non-standard organism in the iGen community.

18
00:02:14,730 --> 00:02:18,510
and just neither piperidine nor bensoid is natively present in Corinobacteria.

19
00:02:19,010 --> 00:02:24,560
We performed tolerance essays to calculate the optimal concentrations of these precursors.

20
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:33,970
To make our project functional and viable, we had to engineer the last protein of our enzyme cascade, as it has a fairly low starting activity for NBP formation.

21
00:02:34,690 --> 00:02:46,610
For this, we first predicted its structure and then its exercise by protein ligand docking using a tool developed by Nobel Prize winner David Baker, which he also spoke about on our international meetup.

22
00:02:48,230 --> 00:02:51,150
